ching updates from Telegram. To fetch updates, you need to\n   595\u2192            either start :attr:`updater` manually or use one of :meth:`run_polling` or\n   596\u2192            :meth:`run_webhook`.\n   597\u2192\n   598\u2192        Tip:\n   599\u2192            When using a custom logic for startup and shutdown of the application, eventual\n   600\u2192            cancellation of pending tasks should happen only `after` :meth:`stop` has been called\n   601\u2192            in order to ensure that the tasks mentioned above are not cancelled prematurely.\n   602\u2192\n   603\u2192        .. seealso::\n   604\u2192            :meth:`stop`\n   605\u2192\n   606\u2192        Raises:\n   607\u2192            :exc:`RuntimeError`: If the application is already running or was not initialized.\n   608\u2192        \"\"\"\n   609\u2192        if self.running:\n   610\u2192            raise RuntimeError(\"This Application is already running!\")\n   611\u2192        self._check_initialized()\n   612\u2192\n   613\u2192        self._running = True\n   614\u2192        self.__update_persistence_event.clear()\n   615\u2192\n   616\u2192        try:\n   617\u2192            if self.persistence:\n   618\u2192                self.__update_persistence_task = asyncio.create_task(\n   619\u2192                    self._persistence_updater(),\n   620\u2192                    name=f\"Application:{self.bot.id}:persistence_updater\",\n   621\u2192                )\n   622\u2192                _LOGGER.debug(\"Loop for updating persistence started\")\n   623\u2192\n   624\u2192            if self._job_queue:\n   625\u2192                await self._job_queue.start()  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n   626\u2192                _LOGGER.debug(\"JobQueue started\")\n   627\u2192\n   628\u2192            self.__update_fetcher_task = asyncio.create_task(\n   629\u2192                self._update_fetcher(), name=f\"Application:{self.bot.id}:update_fetcher\"\n   630\u2192            )\n   631\u21