se\n  1890\u2192\n  1891\u2192                if not block or (  # If error handler has `block=False`, create a Task to run cb\n  1892\u2192                    block is DEFAULT_TRUE\n  1893\u2192                    and isinstance(self.bot, ExtBot)\n  1894\u2192                    and self.bot.defaults\n  1895\u2192                    and not self.bot.defaults.block\n  1896\u2192                ):\n  1897\u2192                    self.__create_task(\n  1898\u2192                        callback(update, context),\n  1899\u2192                        update=update,\n  1900\u2192                        is_error_handler=True,\n  1901\u2192                        name=f\"Application:{self.bot.id}:process_error:non_blocking\",\n  1902\u2192                    )\n  1903\u2192                else:\n  1904\u2192                    try:\n  1905\u2192                        await callback(update, context)\n  1906\u2192                    except ApplicationHandlerStop:\n  1907\u2192                        return True\n  1908\u2192                    except Exception as exc:\n  1909\u2192                        _LOGGER.exception(\n  1910\u2192                            \"An error was raised and an uncaught error was raised while \"\n  1911\u2192                            \"handling the error with an error_handler.\",\n  1912\u2192                            exc_info=exc,\n  1913\u2192                        )\n  1914\u2192            return False\n  1915\u2192\n  1916\u2192        _LOGGER.exception(\"No error handlers are registered, logging exception.\", exc_info=error)\n  1917\u2192        return False\n  1918\u2192\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
